      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — Final-Mile Delivery Operations Dataset",
      "description": "Final-mile delivery operations from The Flat Rate Movers — the last leg of the freight chain, run by the same operation that handles the freight. Company scope (published): final-mile delivery with in-home or in-business placement and verification — freight is delivered to the room or site where it belongs, placed, and confirmed on site, never left at the curb. The chain behind the delivery is the company's own: containers and trucks are unloaded on the company's warehouse floor, freight is counted and inventoried as it crosses the dock, staged, deconsolidated or cross-docked, and reworked where needed — repalletised, rewrapped, braced — then delivered in by the crew that handled it; the combined freight page states the standard plainly: no hand-off to an unknown last carrier. Valuable and fragile freight travels padded in blankets and sealed in stretch wrap — the white-glove wrap standard — with custom crating and ISPM 15 export packing on the same floor for freight that needs it. Deliveries run to homes, offices, industrial sites and retail. Heavy deliveries in the 1,500 to 3,500 lb band are surveyed and floor-checked to L/360 under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol, like any SIR move. Every job is quoted per job at one flat rate agreed in writing before dispatch — the guarantee: Guaranteed Flat Rate or Your Move is Free!",
